==moreThanFive

=died1
#speaker: Athena
Surprisingly lucky! {goodGamblingAttempts} successes out of {totalGamblingAttempts}.

#speaker: Apistos
Glad you noticed.

#speaker: Athena
If only you fought as well as you gamble, my little fish.

#speaker: Apistos
Nothing pleases you... Actually, battles require proper training, while gambling needs no special skills.

#speaker: Athena
Seems to me you're just making excuses for your failures.

#speaker: Apistos
You're so cruel - could at least be happy for your loyal and devoted partner...

#speaker: Athena
I'll be happy when you win the tournament
->DONE

=died2
#speaker: Athena
Sometimes I doubt you're a fish - you're more like a greedy goblin! {goodGamblingAttempts} gambling wins out of {totalGamblingAttempts}?

#speaker: Apistos
I was on fire! Should've bet even more!

#speaker: Athena
Listen here, you petty jackal! Have you forgotten your real purpose?

#speaker: Apistos
"Petty jackal"? Ooh, fresh! Way better than "my little fishy".

#speaker: Athena
Stay focused!

#speaker:Apistos
Right, right... This petty jackal will clean everyone out at cards!

#speaker: Athena
Then march forth and conquer!
->DONE

=died3
#speaker: Athena
Failed again?

#speaker: Apistos
But I'm winning at gambling! {goodGamblingAttempts} wins out of {totalGamblingAttempts}. Lady Luck loves me!

#speaker: Athena
Then maybe you should fight for her instead?

#speaker: Apistos
Oh-ho! Can my ears deceive me? Do I detect... jealousy from the wisest of goddesses?

#speaker: Athena
Wisdom doesn't mean no pride. Praise other gods in my presence again, and you'll walk alone.

#speaker: Apistos
Don't be mad! Where would I find a patron more gracious than you? Truly, I consider you Olympus' finest!

#speaker: Athena
You're not alone in that opinion.

#speaker: Apistos
Ah, so besides jealousy, you've no shortage of modesty either...

#speaker: Athena
HOW DARE YOU!
->DONE

==lessThanFive
=died1
#speaker: Athena
You've been gambling, haven't you?

#speaker: Apistos
Yeah, but I was winning!

#speaker: Athena
Mmm-hmm... Congratulations.

#speaker: Apistos
Wait—how'd you know I was gambling?

#speaker: Athena
You do realize I observe you outside of battles...?

#speaker: Apistos
Oh. Uh-oh...

#speaker: Athena
What?! What else have you done?!

#speaker: Apistos
I dunno, but hey—you're watching anyway, so you tell me!

#speaker: Athena
Stop backtalking. Begone.
->DONE

=died2
#speaker: Apistos
Athena, you won’t believe it—I’ve been killing it at the gambling tables lately!

#speaker: Athena
There’s a saying: "Lucky at dice, unlucky in love."

#speaker: Apistos
Pretty sure you just made that up… But hey, maybe put in a good word with Aphrodite for me? I do still dream of a nice, quiet family life.

#speaker: Athena
Oh I’ll whisper in her ear… AFTER you win the tournament. Now MOVE!
->DONE

=died3
#speaker: Athena
Next time I'll greet you with trumpets!

#speaker: Apistos
Since when are you so generous?

#speaker: Athena
Thought you might need encouragement. So... how much did you lose gambling?

#speaker: Apistos
HA! In your face! I won more than I have - {goodGamblingAttempts} victories!

#speaker: Athena
Ahem. Would you like a medal?

#speaker: Apistos
At least show some admiration!

#speaker: Athena
You seem confused about our roles. I'm the goddess here - you're supposed to worship me.

#speaker: Apistos
Let's table that - right now we're discussing my exceptional luck.

#speaker: Athena
Right, right. Congratulations.

#speaker: Apistos
YOU'RE JUST JEALOUS!

#speaker: Athena
Of what exactly? Remember who you're talking to, mortal. Then ask yourself - what could a goddess envy in you?

#speaker: Apistos
If not my luck, then definitely my charisma. Something you lack, oh mighty goddess.

#speaker: Athena
Remind me to ditch you later.
->DONE

